WEBVTT

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:05.928
Four connection types carry eight message directions, repeated across bridges and towns.

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:10.416
A station reading sends a likelihood over the bridge's shaking.

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:15.568
Each bridge combines the likelihood with damage and road-state information.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.984
The hub combines local messages and sends them to the root.

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:25.024
Observed access constrains possible combinations of road states.

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:33.280
With access evidence, certificate MCMC updates road states. Otherwise, they are drawn directly.

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:39.144
Road samples return to the hub, where elliptical slice sampling updates shaking.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:44.736
Shaking and road samples return to each bridge, updating its damage state.

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:49.744
Shaking samples return to generate unobserved station readings.

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:55.264
Road samples return to system cliques, which evaluate airport access.
